group features/gui
note The 'fit' button of the zoom cluster in the graph canvas's bottom-right corner zooms and pans so the whole graph fits the canvas with a margin, centred, shrinking the font step by step down to the smallest readable size; pressing the zoom percentage beside it sets the zoom back to 100% and centres the selected node. The reader reaches for it after panning and zooming into one part, to see the whole graph again without re-centring by hand. Both sit with the zoom buttons, where map and design apps put them, so each camera control has one place and the toolbar above keeps only layout controls and the legend. The camera otherwise moves only on explicit navigation.

